Description: Retain SONiC's readline-enabled Socat packaging inputs
 Add libreadline-dev to Debian's build dependencies and remove the Debian
 --disable-readline override. The Bazel build separately selects
 --enable-readline; this patch preserves SONiC's Debian-file customization.
Origin: https://github.com/securely1g/sonic-buildimage/blob/af35f605975215872e69dba5a291cb52fd5faafa/src/socat/patch/enable_readline.patch
 The registry normalizes only file headers for its patch reader; the hunks
 are unchanged from that SONiC patch and run after Debian 1.8.0.2-1's series.
Status: Retained downstream SONiC customization; no upstream inclusion is asserted.

diff --git a/debian/rules b/debian/rules
--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -11,9 +11,6 @@
 # upsteram maintains config.h.in manually
 export AUTOHEADER = true
 
-override_dh_auto_configure:
-	dh_auto_configure -- --disable-readline
-
 override_dh_auto_test:
 ifneq (,$(filter $(DEB_HOST_ARCH_OS), linux))
 	dh_auto_test
@@ -24,4 +21,4 @@
 %:
 	dh $@ --with=autoreconf
 
-.PHONY: override_dh_auto_configure override_dh_auto_test
+.PHONY: override_dh_auto_test
diff --git a/debian/control b/debian/control
--- a/debian/control
+++ b/debian/control
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 Section: net
 Priority: optional
 Maintainer: Laszlo Boszormenyi (GCS) <gcs@debian.org>
-Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), libssl-dev, libwrap0-dev, openssl <!nocheck>, net-tools <!nocheck>, iproute2 [linux-any] <!nocheck>, netbase <!nocheck>, procps <!nocheck>
+Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), libssl-dev, libwrap0-dev, libreadline-dev, openssl <!nocheck>, net-tools <!nocheck>, iproute2 [linux-any] <!nocheck>, netbase <!nocheck>, procps <!nocheck>
 Standards-Version: 4.6.2
 Rules-Requires-Root: no
 Homepage: https://www.dest-unreach.org/socat/

